  "id": "quantitative-psychology",
  "term": "quantitative psychology",
  "definition": "Quantitative psychology is an approach that studies psychological attributes by turning them into measurable variables, often with standardized scales and methods modeled on the natural sciences. It mainly looks for causal links between variables from a third-person perspective.",
